    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A county on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> coast, founded in 862, whose counts held most of it from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and a smaller part from the German emperors.</li><li>Its cloth towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghent">Ghent</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ypres">Ypres</a> made it one of the wealthiest and most urbanised regions of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</li><li>It passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> in 1384, then to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, lost its south to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and was annexed by France in 1795.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>’ founder, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-of-flanders">Baldwin Iron Arm</a>, won his county by eloping with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judith-of-france">Judith</a>, a Carolingian princess who had already been married to two kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>, father and son.</p></aside>
    </section>

